	                     The power of our community 
 Important program news:  Foxborough Power Forward will change to new, 2-year prices in November as the program’s current electricity supply contract ends and a new contract takes effect. 
 While changes in the electricity market have increased prices overall, most participants will still pay less than National Grid’s current residential Basic Service price. All participants will enjoy 2 years of price stability. 
 The program has saved Foxborough electricity customers more than $7.5 million compared with National Grid’s prices since launching in 2017, though future savings cannot be guaranteed. 
 See the new prices . 
 Check back soon for the official announcement from the Town of Foxborough. 















			 Did you receive a notice in the mail? 
