	                     The power of our community 
 Important program news:  Foxborough Power Forward will change to new, 2-year prices in November as the program’s current electricity supply contract ends and a new contract takes effect. 
 While changes in the electricity market have increased prices overall, most participants will still pay less than National Grid’s current residential Basic Service price. All participants will enjoy 2 years of price stability. 
 The program has saved Foxborough electricity customers more than $7.5 million compared with National Grid’s prices since launching in 2017, though future savings cannot be guaranteed. 
 See the new prices . 
 Check back soon for the official announcement from the Town of Foxborough. 















			 Did you receive a notice in the mail? 
 Learn more 


			 Not sure where to start? 

 Download a 2-page program overview 













		 Foxborough Power Forward is a group electricity buying program for Foxborough residents and businesses. Using the purchasing power of our community, the program provides: 

 Two consumer-friendly electricity supply options 
 Stable and consistent pricing until November 2028 
 The ability to leave at any time with no fee or penalty 

 More than 200 other Massachusetts communities have similar programs. 
 Program benefits 






 Two consumer-friendly options 
 Foxborough Power Forward offers two options for the electricity supply price on your National Grid bill. As a new participant, you will be automatically enrolled in Power Forward Standard. Power Forward Green provides 100% of your electricity from new, renewable sources and is available by request. Make the choice that’s right for you! 

 Learn more about program options and prices .   Need help deciding?  Contact customer support . 
 Foxborough Power Forward offers long-term prices, while National Grid’s prices change seasonally.  Use the calculator  to compare Foxborough Power Forward prices with National Grid’s average prices. 





		 No interruption in service  
 Through Foxborough Power Forward, the Town has selected First Point Power as our electricity supplier (the company that puts electricity on the grid for us) and locked in long-term pricing for the electricity supply price on our bills. But National Grid remains Foxborough’s electric utility and continues to handle our billing, address power outages, and deliver our electricity with no interruption.  Learn more about how aggregation works . 

   





